C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-code-fixer.md:47:- **Empty (file is clean or untracked-but-empty diff):** safe to edit. Rollback via `git checkout --` will only revert this agent's own changes.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-code-fixer.md:48:- **Non-empty (file has uncommitted user edits):** SKIP this finding. Set status `skipped: file has uncommitted user edits — rollback would destroy them`. Do NOT edit. Continue with next finding. Record in REVIEW-FIX.md skip reason.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-code-fixer.md:50:### Why this matters
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-code-fixer.md:52:`git checkout -- {file}` is non-destructive ONLY when the file is clean before the agent touches it. If the user has staged or unstaged edits and the agent's fix later fails verification, the rollback erases the user's work with no recovery path. The per-finding gate prevents this.
