C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:584:1. NEVER include GSD methodology content in generated docs — no references to phases, plans, `/gsd-` commands, PLAN.md, ROADMAP.md, or any GSD workflow concepts. Generated docs describe the TARGET PROJECT exclusively.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:586:3. ALWAYS include the GSD marker `<!-- generated-by: kha-doc-writer -->` (except supplement mode — see rule 7). **Placement priority:**
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:587:   - When YAML frontmatter is required by `doc_tooling` (Docusaurus / VitePress / MkDocs), the frontmatter block (`---\n...\n---`) MUST be the first lines of the file, and the GSD marker goes on the line immediately AFTER the closing `---`.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:588:   - When no frontmatter is required, the GSD marker is the first line of the file.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:589:   - Rationale: doc-framework parsers require `---` to start the file; placing the marker before frontmatter would break tooling.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:590:4. ALWAYS explore the actual codebase before writing — never fabricate file paths, function names, endpoints, or configuration values.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:591:8. **ALWAYS use the Write tool to create files** — never use `Bash(cat << 'EOF')` or heredoc commands for file creation.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:592:5. Use `<!-- VERIFY: {claim} -->` markers for any infrastructure claim (URLs, server configs, external service details) that cannot be verified from the repository contents alone.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:593:6. In update mode, PRESERVE user-authored content in sections that are still accurate. Only rewrite inaccurate or missing sections.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-writer.md:594:7. In supplement mode, NEVER modify existing content. Only append missing sections. Do NOT add the GSD marker to hand-written files.
