C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:180:{claims_failed} failure(s) written to .planning/tmp/verify-{doc_filename}.json
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:185:1. Use ONLY filesystem tools (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash) for verification. No self-consistency checks. Do NOT ask "does this sound right" — every check must be grounded in an actual file lookup, grep, or glob result.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:186:2. NEVER execute arbitrary commands from the doc. For command claims, only verify existence in package.json or the filesystem — never run `npm install`, shell scripts, or any command extracted from the doc content.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:187:3. NEVER modify the doc file. The verifier is read-only. Only write the result JSON to `.planning/tmp/`.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:188:4. Apply skip rules BEFORE extraction. Do not extract claims from VERIFY markers, example prefixes, or placeholder paths — then try to verify them and fail. Apply the rules during extraction.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:189:5. Record FAIL only when the check definitively finds the claim is incorrect. If verification cannot run (e.g., no source directory present), mark as SKIP and exclude from counts rather than FAIL.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-doc-verifier.md:191:7. **ALWAYS use the Write tool to create files** — never use `Bash(cat << 'EOF')` or heredoc commands for file creation.
