C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:417:**When:** Code constructs paths, URLs, keys, or references from variables — and the constructed value might not point where you expect.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:419:**The trap:** You read code that builds a path like `path.join(configDir, 'hooks')` and assume it's correct because it looks reasonable. But you never verified that the constructed path matches where another part of the system actually writes/reads.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:422:1. Find the code that **produces** the value (writer/installer/creator)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:423:2. Find the code that **consumes** the value (reader/checker/validator)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:425:4. Check every variable in the path construction — where does each come from? What's its actual value at runtime?
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:430:- Variable is derived differently in two places (e.g., one adds a subdirectory, the other doesn't)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:431:- Template placeholder (`{{VERSION}}`) not substituted in all code paths
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:433:**Example:** Stale hook warning persists after update
