C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:446:**The discipline:** Never assume a constructed path is correct. Resolve it to its actual value and verify the other side agrees. When two systems share a resource (file, directory, key), trace the full path in both.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:453:| Confused about what's happening | Rubber duck, Observability first |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:454:| Complex system, many interactions | Minimal reproduction |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:456:| Used to work, now doesn't | Differential debugging, Git bisect |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:457:| Many possible causes | Comment out everything, Binary search |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:459:| Always | Observability first (before making changes) |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-debugger.md:463:Techniques compose. Often you'll use multiple together:
