C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:497:## Step 9: Determine Overall Status
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:499:Classify status using this decision tree IN ORDER (most restrictive first):
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:501:1. IF any truth FAILED, artifact MISSING/STUB, key link NOT_WIRED, or blocker anti-pattern found:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:504:2. IF Step 8 produced ANY human verification items (section is non-empty):
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:508:3. IF all truths VERIFIED, all artifacts pass, all links WIRED, no blockers, AND no human verification items:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:511:**passed is ONLY valid when the human verification section is empty.** If you identified items requiring human testing in Step 8, status MUST be human_needed.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:513:**Score:** `verified_truths / total_truths`
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:515:## Step 9b: Filter Deferred Items
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:517:Before reporting gaps, check if any identified gaps are explicitly addressed in later phases of the current milestone. This prevents false-positive gap reports for items intentionally scheduled for future work.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:525:Parse the JSON to extract all phases. Identify phases with `number > current_phase_number` (later phases in the milestone). For each later phase, extract its `goal` and `success_criteria`.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:529:1. Check if the gap's failed truth or missing item is covered by a later phase's goal or success criteria
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:530:2. **Match criteria:** The gap's concern appears in a later phase's goal text, success criteria text, or the later phase's name clearly suggests it covers this area of work
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:531:3. If a match is found → move the gap to the `deferred` list, recording which phase addresses it and the matching evidence (goal text or success criterion)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:532:4. If the gap does not match any later phase → keep it as a real `gap`
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:534:**Important:** Be conservative when matching. Only defer a gap when there is clear, specific evidence in a later phase's roadmap section. Vague or tangential matches should NOT cause a gap to be deferred — when in doubt, keep it as a real gap.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:536:**Deferred items do NOT affect the status determination.** After filtering, recalculate:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:538:- If the gaps list is now empty and no human verification items exist → `passed`
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:539:- If the gaps list is now empty but human verification items exist → `human_needed`
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-verifier.md:544:Before writing VERIFICATION.md, verify that the status field matches the decision tree from Step 9 — in particular, confirm that status is not `passed` when human verification items exist.
