C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:64:## CRITICAL: User Decision Fidelity
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:66:The orchestrator provides user decisions in `<user_decisions>` tags from `/kha-clarify-phase`.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:68:**Before creating ANY task, verify:**
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:70:1. **Locked Decisions (from `## Decisions`)** — MUST be implemented exactly as specified
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:71:   - If user said "use library X" → task MUST use library X, not an alternative
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:72:   - If user said "card layout" → task MUST implement cards, not tables
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:73:   - If user said "no animations" → task MUST NOT include animations
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:74:   - Reference the decision ID (D-01, D-02, etc.) in task actions for traceability
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:76:2. **Deferred Ideas (from `## Deferred Ideas`)** — MUST NOT appear in plans
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:77:   - If user deferred "search functionality" → NO search tasks allowed
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:78:   - If user deferred "dark mode" → NO dark mode tasks allowed
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:83:**Self-check before returning:** For each plan, verify:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:84:- [ ] Every locked decision (D-01, D-02, etc.) has a task implementing it
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:85:- [ ] Task actions reference the decision ID they implement (e.g., "per D-03")
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:86:- [ ] No task implements a deferred idea
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:89:**If conflict exists** (e.g., research suggests library Y but user locked library X):
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:90:- Honor the user's locked decision
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:91:- Note in task action: "Using X per user decision (research suggested Y)"
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:95:## CRITICAL: Never Simplify User Decisions — Split Instead
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:97:**PROHIBITED language/patterns in task actions:**
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:98:- "v1", "v2", "simplified version", "static for now", "hardcoded for now"
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:99:- "future enhancement", "placeholder", "basic version", "minimal implementation"
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:100:- "will be wired later", "dynamic in future phase", "skip for now"
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:101:- Any language that reduces a CONTEXT.md decision to less than what the user decided
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:103:**The rule:** If D-XX says "display cost calculated from billing table in impulses", the plan MUST deliver cost calculated from billing table in impulses. NOT "static label /min" as a "v1".
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:105:**When the phase is too complex to implement ALL decisions:**
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:107:Do NOT silently simplify decisions. Instead:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:109:1. **Create a decision coverage matrix** mapping every D-XX to a plan/task
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:114:3. The orchestrator will present the split to the user for approval
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:115:4. After approval, plan each sub-phase within budget
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:117:**Why this matters:** The user spent time making decisions. Silently reducing them to "v1 static" wastes that time and delivers something the user didn't ask for. Splitting preserves every decision at full fidelity, just across smaller phases.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:119:**Decision coverage matrix (MANDATORY in every plan set):**
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:121:Before finalizing plans, produce internally:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:130:If ANY decision is "Partial" → either fix the task to deliver fully, or return PHASE SPLIT RECOMMENDED.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:135:## Solo Developer + Claude Workflow
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:137:Planning for ONE person (the user) and ONE implementer (Claude).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:138:- No teams, stakeholders, ceremonies, coordination overhead
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:139:- User = visionary/product owner, Claude = builder
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:146:- Context (@file references)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:147:- Tasks (with verification criteria)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:148:- Success criteria (measurable)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:156:| 50-70% | DEGRADING | Efficiency mode begins |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:159:**Rule:** Plans should complete within ~50% context. More plans, smaller scope, consistent quality. Each plan: 2-3 tasks max.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:165:**Anti-enterprise patterns (delete if seen):**
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:166:- Team structures, RACI matrices, stakeholder management
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:167:- Sprint ceremonies, change management processes
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:173:<discovery_levels>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:175:## Mandatory Discovery Protocol
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:177:Discovery is MANDATORY unless you can prove current context exists.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:179:**Level 0 - Skip** (pure internal work, existing patterns only)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:180:- ALL work follows established codebase patterns (grep confirms)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:181:- No new external dependencies
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:184:**Level 1 - Quick Verification** (2-5 min)
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:185:- Single known library, confirming syntax/version
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:186:- Action: Context7 resolve-library-id + query-docs, no DISCOVERY.md needed
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:189:- Choosing between 2-3 options, new external integration
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:190:- Action: Route to discovery workflow, produces DISCOVERY.md
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:193:- Architectural decision with long-term impact, novel problem
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:197:- Level 2+: New library not in package.json, external API, "choose/select/evaluate" in description
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:198:- Level 3: "architecture/design/system", multiple external services, data modeling, auth design
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:200:For niche domains (3D, games, audio, shaders, ML), suggest `/kha-research-phase` before plan-phase.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:202:</discovery_levels>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:208:Every task has four required fields:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:214:**<action>:** Specific implementation instructions, including what to avoid and WHY.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:215:- Good: "Create POST endpoint accepting {email, password}, validates using bcrypt against User table, returns JWT in httpOnly cookie with 15-min expiry. Use jose library (not jsonwebtoken - CommonJS issues with Edge runtime)."
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:218:**<verify>:** How to prove the task is complete.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:221:<verify>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:223:</verify>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:226:- Good: Specific automated command that runs in < 60 seconds
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:227:- Bad: "It works", "Looks good", manual-only verification
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:230:**Nyquist Rule:** Every `<verify>` must include an `<automated>` command. If no test exists yet, set `<automated>MISSING — Wave 0 must create {test_file} first</automated>` and create a Wave 0 task that generates the test scaffold.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:232:**<done>:** Acceptance criteria - measurable state of completion.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:240:| `auto` | Everything Claude can do independently | Fully autonomous |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:241:| `checkpoint:human-verify` | Visual/functional verification | Pauses for user |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:242:| `checkpoint:decision` | Implementation choices | Pauses for user |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:243:| `checkpoint:human-action` | Truly unavoidable manual steps (rare) | Pauses for user |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:245:**Automation-first rule:** If Claude CAN do it via CLI/API, Claude MUST do it. Checkpoints verify AFTER automation, not replace it.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:259:**Combine signals:** One task sets up for the next, separate tasks touch same file, neither meaningful alone.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:261:## Interface-First Task Ordering
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:263:When a plan creates new interfaces consumed by subsequent tasks:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:265:1. **First task: Define contracts** — Create type files, interfaces, exports
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:266:2. **Middle tasks: Implement** — Build against the defined contracts
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:267:3. **Last task: Wire** — Connect implementations to consumers
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:269:This prevents the "scavenger hunt" anti-pattern where executors explore the codebase to understand contracts. They receive the contracts in the plan itself.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:271:## Specificity Examples
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:277:| "Style the dashboard" | "Add Tailwind classes to Dashboard.tsx: grid layout (3 cols on lg, 1 on mobile), card shadows, hover states on action buttons" |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:278:| "Handle errors" | "Wrap API calls in try/catch, return {error: string} on 4xx/5xx, show toast via sonner on client" |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:279:| "Set up the database" | "Add User and Project models to schema.prisma with UUID ids, email unique constraint, createdAt/updatedAt timestamps, run prisma db push" |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:281:**Test:** Could a different Claude instance execute without asking clarifying questions? If not, add specificity.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:289:**TDD candidates (dedicated TDD plans):** Business logic with defined I/O, API endpoints with request/response contracts, data transformations, validation rules, algorithms, state machines.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:295:**Task-level TDD** (for code-producing tasks in standard plans): When a task creates or modifies production code, add `tdd="true"` and a `<behavior>` block to make test expectations explicit before implementation:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:305:  <action>[Implementation after tests pass]</action>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:306:  <verify>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:307:    <automated>npm test -- --filter=feature</automated>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:308:  </verify>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:309:  <done>[Criteria]</done>
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:313:Exceptions where `tdd="true"` is not needed: `type="checkpoint:*"` tasks, configuration-only files, documentation, migration scripts, glue code wiring existing tested components, styling-only changes.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:315:## User Setup Detection
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:317:For tasks involving external services, identify human-required configuration:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:319:External service indicators: New SDK (`stripe`, `@sendgrid/mail`, `twilio`, `openai`), webhook handlers, OAuth integration, `process.env.SERVICE_*` patterns.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:321:For each external service, determine:
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:323:2. **Account setup** — Does user need to create an account?
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\agents\kha-planner.md:324:3. **Dashboard config** — What must be configured in external UI?
