C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:142:Failure mode: `record_invocation` raises `ValueError` only on bad sid / agent_name (path traversal, empty). Wrap in `try/except ValueError` if defensive; do NOT swallow other exceptions (the underlying `jsonl_append` is already fail-soft via `lib.telemetry_log`).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:145:- Do NOT implement accepted decisions. That is the next user action.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:147:- Do NOT spawn sub-tasks beyond the three debate agents (planner, critic, architect).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:148:- Do NOT inline Planner/Critic/Architect logic in this orchestrator — always go through the Agent tool so subagent prompts stay isolated.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:153:- events log: `events.jsonl` — append-only event sourcing (`proposal`, `critique`, `verdict`, `convergence`).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:154:- per-generation actor outputs embedded in `payload` of each event.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:155:- final user-facing message: numbered `ontology_snapshot.fields`, `accepted_decisions` checklist, absolute path to `events.jsonl`, `self_doubt_note` verbatim.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:156:- status: `converged` (Architect approved + snapshot hash stable) | `hard_cap` (4 gen reached without convergence) | `early_hard_cap` (v15.40 — step 4.5 stagnation/oscillation/blocker_plateau detector fired before gen=4) | `aborted_parse_failure` (JSON parse failed twice on same actor) | `aborted_no_topic` (empty argument).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:160:- **empty topic argument**: ask user once for one-sentence design decision; abort (`aborted_no_topic`) if reply is also empty. No session dir created.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:161:- **actor JSON parse failure**: retry the same actor with the same prompt ONCE. On second failure, log `parse_failure` event and escalate to user (`aborted_parse_failure`). Do NOT silently substitute a default verdict.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:162:- **Architect verdict missing/invalid**: treated as `parse_failure` (above).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:163:- **fast-path bypass eligibility**: if gen 1 Critic is skipped per fast-path rules (empty `open_questions` + STRICT_DESIGN_KEYWORDS keyword + no `critic_feedback`) AND Architect approves the Critic-less proposal → converged. Otherwise fall through to gen 2 with full Critic. Gen-1-only convergence WITHOUT fast-path is a documentation contract, not a rule — never short-circuit on first approval alone.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:164:- **hard cap (4 generations)**: print every gen's verdict summary + "convergence failed after 4 generations — user decision required". Implementation is then user's responsibility — engine does NOT auto-implement.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:168:- preflight: topic argument non-empty after trim; CLAUDE_HOME resolves; `state/debates/` writable.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:169:- success criteria: convergence event written with `status=converged`. For non-fast-path: previous-and-current gen's `ontology_snapshot.fields` SHA-1 hash matches AND verdict=`approved`.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:170:- abort triggers: empty topic after re-prompt; double parse failure on any actor; hard cap reached.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:174:- checkpoint: `events.jsonl` is the canonical replay log. Each generation's `proposal`/`critique`/`verdict` events let an external caller reconstruct any prior state.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:175:- resume command: not implemented at command level — re-running `/harness-debate <topic>` mints a NEW session id. Manual resume = read prior `events.jsonl` and feed last verdict's `ontology_snapshot` as `prior_generation` to a fresh Planner call.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:176:- idempotent: NO at session level (each invocation = new sid). YES per generation (re-running the same prompt at the same gen with the same input deterministically reaches the same verdict barring LLM nondeterminism).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:177:- stall detection: gen counter monotonic — if a generation passes without producing a `verdict` event within reasonable wall time, treat as failure (no auto-retry beyond actor-level retry above).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:179:## Boundary with other commands
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:181:- vs `harness-autopilot`: this **decides**, autopilot **executes**. Debate output (accepted_decisions) is autopilot's input.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:182:- vs `harness-ralph`: this is design convergence; ralph is implementation/test verification persistence.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:183:- vs `harness-team`: team fans out the SAME prompt to multiple AIs for diverse opinions; debate runs DIFFERENT roles (Planner/Critic/Architect) for structured convergence on a single decision.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-debate.md:184:- vs `harness-interview`: interview gathers context (questions); debate decides on a topic given context.
