C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:350:- checkpoint: super-session via `engine.orchestrator` — `state/orchestrator/<sid>/events.jsonl` is canonical (replayable), `phase-tree.md` is derived (regenerated each transition), `child_sids.json` maps phase_id → child engine sid (debate/ralph/team) via atomic write.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:351:- resume command: `/harness-autopilot --resume <sid>` is first-class. `engine.orchestrator.load_session(sid)` replays events.jsonl, returns the root phase + child_sids. Caller reads `next_action` on the root and jumps to the matching phase. B5 cold-start: `FileNotFoundError` → `aborted_resume_unknown_sid`. B5 fail-closed: corrupt `child_sids.json` → `RuntimeError` (never silent reset).
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:352:- idempotent: per-invocation. Same sid resume reads the same events log; new invocation without `--resume` mints a new sid. Phase 1 commits remain git-level idempotent.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:353:- stall detection: phase-level — debate gen counter + ralph iteration counter. Super-session has no global wall-clock timeout in MVP; D7 adds a researcher-step timeout when Phase 2 lands.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:354:- TTY fallback (D4b): on `--resume <sid>` where the sid dir already exists, `engine.orchestrator.confirm_resume_or_new(sid)` checks `sys.stdin.isatty()`; non-tty (autopilot child spawn) → `'resume'` default; tty → interactive `r/n/a` prompt.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:356:## Boundary with other commands
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:358:- vs `harness-debate`: this RUNS debate as Phase 0 then continues to executor + validator + ralph. Debate alone is decision-only, no implementation.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:359:- vs `harness-ralph`: this runs ralph as Phase 3 (validator FAIL recovery). Ralph alone presumes you already have implementation + validators.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:360:- vs `harness-ultrawork`: this is debate+execute+verify+fix for a SINGLE goal; ultrawork is parallel waves of independent slices, no validator loop.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:361:- vs `kha-run-milestone`: this runs ad-hoc single goal end-to-end; run-milestone iterates roadmap-driven phases sequentially.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\commands\harness-autopilot.md:362:- vs `/goal` (Claude Code 공식, 2026-Q1+): `/goal`은 session-scoped prompt-based Stop hook으로 LLM(Haiku)이 매 턴 prose stop-condition을 평가. autopilot은 자체 Stop hook `scripts/handlers/stop/autopilot_continue.py` (debate-1778224899-c24de4 D3''='single')로 **deterministic state machine** 기반 multi-turn loop을 운영. 두 hook은 settings.json `Stop` 배열에서 **병렬 작동** — `/goal`은 prose 판정, autopilot은 `<autopilot mode='execute' sid=... iter=...>` tag 기반 state 진행. 사용자가 `/goal "..."`을 추가로 등록하면 두 조건 모두 충족해야 turn이 자연 종료. autopilot이 활성이면 `autopilot_continue.py`가 우선 (response_guard도 D3'' merge로 흡수). 공식 `/goal` 명세 주의사항: ① 500-turn 하드캡 없음 (그건 커뮤니티 클론 jthack/claude-goal). 사용자가 prose에 "or stop after N turns" 명시. ② `/goal pause` 서브커맨드 없음. `clear/stop/off/reset/none/cancel`만 존재. ③ nesting=replacement (두 번째 `/goal`이 첫 번째 덮어씀). ④ `--resume`/`--continue`는 active goal 복원하지만 turn-count/timer/token baseline은 리셋.
