C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:116:## Why Order Matters
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:118:### "I'll write tests after to verify it works"
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:143:### "Tests after achieve the same goals — it's spirit not ritual"
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:144:**No.** Tests-after는 "What does this do?" 답변. Tests-first는 "What SHOULD this do?" 답변.
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:153:| "I'll test after" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:154:| "Tests after achieve same goals" | Tests-after = "what does this do?" Tests-first = "what should this do?" |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:156:| "Deleting X hours is wasteful" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:157:| "Keep as reference, write tests first" | You'll adapt it. That's testing after. Delete means delete. |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:160:| "TDD will slow me down" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |
C:\Users\rudtn\zeus\.runtime\absorption\sources\baldrix\pinned\skills\_common\test-driven-development.md:161:| "Manual test faster" | Manual doesn't prove edge cases. You'll re-test every change. |
